1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,442
It's a Sunday night.

2
00:00:01,342 --> 00:00:03,318
You spread every bill you owe across

3
00:00:03,218 --> 00:00:04,256
the kitchen table.

4
00:00:04,456 --> 00:00:05,722
And for the first time,

5
00:00:05,622 --> 00:00:06,636
you add it all up.

6
00:00:06,986 --> 00:00:08,539
Fourteen thousand dollars.

7
00:00:08,739 --> 00:00:11,051
Your stomach drops. Just for a second.

8
00:00:11,401 --> 00:00:13,347
A twelve hundred dollar medical bill.

9
00:00:13,547 --> 00:00:15,796
A five thousand five hundred dollar car

10
00:00:15,696 --> 00:00:17,008
loan at seven percent.

11
00:00:17,358 --> 00:00:19,308
And a credit card with seven thousand

12
00:00:19,208 --> 00:00:20,709
three hundred dollars on it.

13
00:00:20,909 --> 00:00:22,724
At twenty five percent interest.

14
00:00:23,074 --> 00:00:25,369
Your friend Jake has almost the same pile.

15
00:00:25,569 --> 00:00:27,572
His plan? Pay the minimums and hope.

16
00:00:27,922 --> 00:00:29,570
Your friend Mia just texted you.

17
00:00:29,770 --> 00:00:31,453
I'm doing the snowball method.

18
00:00:31,353 --> 00:00:32,139
Want to join?

19
00:00:32,489 --> 00:00:34,486
So tonight, you do something different.

20
00:00:34,686 --> 00:00:36,697
You run the numbers on all three

21
00:00:36,597 --> 00:00:38,787
plans. Jake's. Mia's. And one more.

22
00:00:39,137 --> 00:00:41,845
Plan one. Jake's plan. Minimums only.

23
00:00:42,045 --> 00:00:44,137
That's four hundred thirty dollars a month.

24
00:00:44,487 --> 00:00:46,572
The medical bill? Gone in two years.

25
00:00:46,772 --> 00:00:48,764
The car loan? About two and a half.

26
00:00:49,114 --> 00:00:50,329
But that credit card?

27
00:00:50,529 --> 00:00:52,133
At one hundred eighty a month,

28
00:00:52,033 --> 00:00:53,436
it takes over seven years.

29
00:00:53,786 --> 00:00:56,298
Because every month, about one hundred fifty

30
00:00:56,198 --> 00:00:58,491
dollars of his payment is just interest.

31
00:00:58,691 --> 00:01:00,897
He pays, and the balance barely moves.

32
00:01:01,247 --> 00:01:02,960
Total interest on Jake's plan?

33
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:05,367
Almost nine thousand five hundred dollars.

34
00:01:05,717 --> 00:01:08,427
Nine thousand five hundred dollars. For nothing.

35
00:01:08,627 --> 00:01:09,815
That's a used car.

36
00:01:09,715 --> 00:01:11,327
Or a full emergency fund.

37
00:01:11,677 --> 00:01:12,888
So before any method,

38
00:01:12,788 --> 00:01:13,893
you need one thing.

39
00:01:14,093 --> 00:01:15,676
A little extra every month.

40
00:01:16,026 --> 00:01:18,961
You cancel two streaming services you barely watch.

41
00:01:19,161 --> 00:01:20,356
That's thirty dollars.

42
00:01:20,706 --> 00:01:22,595
You cook three more dinners at home

43
00:01:22,495 --> 00:01:24,282
each week instead of ordering in.

44
00:01:24,482 --> 00:01:26,354
That's about one hundred dollars a month.

45
00:01:26,704 --> 00:01:28,473
And you sell the bike you haven't

46
00:01:28,373 --> 00:01:29,333
ridden in a year,

47
00:01:29,233 --> 00:01:31,760
then call your phone company for a cheaper plan.

48
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,408
Another forty a month.

49
00:01:33,758 --> 00:01:35,642
One hundred seventy dollars extra.

50
00:01:35,842 --> 00:01:37,402
Now you can pay six hundred a

51
00:01:37,302 --> 00:01:38,862
month instead of four thirty.

52
00:01:39,212 --> 00:01:40,694
Plan two. Mia's plan.

53
00:01:40,594 --> 00:01:41,878
The debt snowball.

54
00:01:42,078 --> 00:01:43,930
Pay the minimums on everything.

55
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:46,700
Then throw all the extra at the smallest balance.

56
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:49,841
For Mia, that's the twelve hundred dollar medical bill.

57
00:01:50,041 --> 00:01:51,741
And six months later, it's gone.

58
00:01:52,091 --> 00:01:53,761
That first win feels amazing.

59
00:01:53,961 --> 00:01:56,543
Now that whole payment rolls onto the car loan.

60
00:01:56,893 --> 00:01:58,996
The car is paid off in month seventeen.

61
00:01:59,196 --> 00:02:01,553
Then everything rolls onto the credit card.

62
00:02:01,903 --> 00:02:03,949
Thirty months. Completely debt free.

63
00:02:04,149 --> 00:02:06,745
About three thousand eight hundred dollars in interest.

64
00:02:07,095 --> 00:02:09,312
Plan three. The one you keep looking at.

65
00:02:09,512 --> 00:02:10,615
The debt avalanche.

66
00:02:10,965 --> 00:02:13,481
Same minimums. Same six hundred dollars.

67
00:02:13,681 --> 00:02:15,633
But the extra goes to the highest

68
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:18,216
interest rate first. Not the smallest balance.

69
00:02:18,566 --> 00:02:20,435
For you, that's the credit card.

70
00:02:20,335 --> 00:02:21,540
Twenty five percent.

71
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:23,711
It's the debt that grows the fastest.

72
00:02:24,061 --> 00:02:26,270
The hard part? For almost two years,

73
00:02:26,170 --> 00:02:27,383
no debt disappears.

74
00:02:27,583 --> 00:02:29,710
You just watch the card balance shrink.

75
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:30,645
Month after month.

76
00:02:30,995 --> 00:02:32,653
Jake asks why you're bothering.

77
00:02:32,853 --> 00:02:34,935
You just smile. Every dollar you save

78
00:02:34,835 --> 00:02:37,238
on interest is a dollar that works for you.

79
00:02:37,588 --> 00:02:40,253
Month twenty eight. The credit card hits zero.

80
00:02:40,453 --> 00:02:42,459
The big one. The scary one. Gone.

81
00:02:42,809 --> 00:02:44,890
One month later, the rest is gone too.

82
00:02:45,090 --> 00:02:46,919
Twenty nine months. Debt free.

83
00:02:47,269 --> 00:02:48,126
So who won?

84
00:02:48,326 --> 00:02:49,973
Here are the real numbers.

85
00:02:49,873 --> 00:02:50,747
Side by side.

86
00:02:51,097 --> 00:02:53,802
Jake's minimums: about seven and a half years.

87
00:02:54,002 --> 00:02:56,614
Nine thousand five hundred dollars in interest.

88
00:02:56,964 --> 00:02:58,799
Mia's snowball: thirty months.

89
00:02:58,999 --> 00:03:01,109
Three thousand eight hundred in interest.

90
00:03:01,459 --> 00:03:03,414
Your avalanche: twenty nine months.

91
00:03:03,614 --> 00:03:05,863
About two thousand nine hundred in interest.

92
00:03:06,213 --> 00:03:08,515
The avalanche saved you about nine hundred

93
00:03:08,415 --> 00:03:10,140
dollars more than the snowball.

94
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:11,809
And it finished one month sooner.

95
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:14,133
But here's the part nobody tells you.

96
00:03:14,333 --> 00:03:16,538
The difference between the two methods is

97
00:03:16,438 --> 00:03:18,592
small. The difference from Jake is huge.

98
00:03:18,942 --> 00:03:20,746
The snowball gives you quick wins.

99
00:03:20,946 --> 00:03:23,529
Research suggests those small wins help people

100
00:03:23,429 --> 00:03:24,608
stick with the plan.

101
00:03:24,958 --> 00:03:26,472
The avalanche costs less.

102
00:03:26,672 --> 00:03:27,999
But only if you don't quit in

103
00:03:27,899 --> 00:03:28,676
the long middle.

104
00:03:29,026 --> 00:03:30,932
So pick the one you'll actually finish.

105
00:03:31,132 --> 00:03:34,492
Need motivation? Snowball. Love the math? Avalanche.

106
00:03:34,842 --> 00:03:37,206
Either way, the real secret is the same.

107
00:03:37,406 --> 00:03:40,195
Find extra money, and never stop at the minimum.

108
00:03:40,545 --> 00:03:41,883
Twenty nine months later,

109
00:03:41,783 --> 00:03:43,071
it's Sunday night again.

110
00:03:43,271 --> 00:03:45,178
The kitchen table is empty.

111
00:03:45,078 --> 00:03:47,053
No bills. Just a cup of tea.

112
00:03:47,403 --> 00:03:49,186
And that six hundred dollars a month?

113
00:03:49,386 --> 00:03:51,243
Now it goes straight into your savings.

114
00:03:51,593 --> 00:03:53,579
If this helped, subscribe for a new

115
00:03:53,479 --> 00:03:55,088
simple money move every day.

116
00:03:55,288 --> 00:03:56,889
And tell me in the comments.

117
00:03:56,789 --> 00:03:59,034
Are you team snowball or team avalanche?
